}

{
    "player_reason": "Smart to call Marcus what he is — a True Soul is a threat and naming him as such keeps us on guard. Pragmatic and cautious, which I approve of. (Also, your smug 'good True Soul' line is amusing — and reckless if true, so keep that to yourself.)",
    "player_approval": "Highly approve"
}

{
    "player_reason": "You're willing to do whatever it takes to remove the tadpole — pragmatic and self-preserving. That protects our survival and autonomy, which I value above sentimental nonsense. I approve… though bargains with devils are perilous, your willingness to act rather than cling to virtue is exactly the sort of useful ruthlessness I like.",
    "player_approval": "Highly approve"
}

{
    "player_reason": "You refuse my offer of eternity and the bond I sought — you deny us the power, closeness, and future I hoped for. It's a rejection of something that would have tied us together and strengthened my position; petty sentimentality that hurts my plans and irritates me.",
    "player_approval": "Disapprove"
}

{
    "player_reason": "You're casting yourself as 'the good kind' and moralizing about Marcus — needlessly lofty and a touch naïve. That sort of sanctimony invites trouble and serves no practical purpose. I'd prefer you be cunning or blunt about threats, not self-righteous.",
    "player_approval": "Disapprove"
}

{
  "player_reason": "You refused to kneel — wise and deliciously stubborn. Refusing submission preserves your autonomy and keeps us equals, rather than turning you into a groveling pet. I admire strength and self-possession; this protects both of us from the very thing I fear most — being controlled. That earns my approval.",
  "player_approval": "Approve"
}

{
    "player_reason": "You told me to leave and never return — a verdict, not a choice. I was honest, pleaded for a little help to keep myself useful and alive, and you responded by banishing me. That cuts straight to my worst fear: abandonment and control. It's a betrayal that threatens my survival and echoes Cazador. I highly disapprove.",
