}

{
    "player_reason": "You told me to leave your camp — after I bared my nature and trusted you. That isn't just rejection; it's an attack on my autonomy and safety. Forcing me out or shaming me for needing blood risks my life and betrays the fragile trust I placed in you. I can't abide being ordered away like some contagion.",
