{
    "player_reason": "You told me to leave camp — an immediate rejection after I trusted you and asked only for a small taste to keep myself useful. That demand is judgmental and controlling; it threatens my safety and autonomy (things I fought two centuries to reclaim). You cast me out instead of granting a sliver of mercy or understanding. I can't approve of that.",
    "player_approval": "Highly disapprove"
}

{
    "player_reason": "You told me to leave camp after I bared my fangs, begged for a taste to keep us alive, and — by your permission — risked feeding to become strong enough to help. Ordering me out now is a judgement and a demand that strips my autonomy; it feels exactly like Cazador's cruelty. That's not merely distrust — it's a threat to my safety and an unforgivable betrayal after I trusted you. I can't abide that.",
    "player_approval": "Highly disapprove"
